{"availability":"available","full":"AtomicBot-ai/atomic-agent","name":"atomic-agent","description":"Atomic Agent is a local-first AI agent. Runs open-weight models on your own machine via llama.cpp.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"TypeScript","stars":3334,"forks":273,"created":"2026-04-21T21:34:51Z","updated":"2026-10-15T12:14:54Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://atomicagent.io","topics":["agents","ai-agent","browser-automation","cli","gbnf","gguf","hermes-agent","llama-cpp","llm","local-ai-agent","local-first","local-llm","mcp","nodejs","openai","openclaw","playwright","tui","typescript"],"demo":"https://cal.com/atomicagent/demo","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T12:58:20.929Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T12:58:20.929Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T12:58:20.929Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T23:11:43.665Z","stars":3193,"forks":261},{"at":"2026-10-15T12:58:20.929Z","stars":3334,"forks":273}],"technologies":["React","Node.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A local-first AI agent that runs on your machine, with local or cloud models.","Drives your browser, edits files, runs approved commands, and remembers context across sessions. Open source, running on our TurboQuant llama.cpp for +30-50% throughput on small local models.","[](#benchmarks) []( []( [](package.json) [](LICENSE) []( []("],"features":["State lives on your disk. Sessions, memory, tasks, traces, skills, browser profile, config, and .env secrets live under as plain files and SQLite databases. See Privacy and Egress for what can leave the machine and how…","No API costs with local models. Run quantized models locally through llama.cpp. Bring your own llama-server or let the CLI manage one. Cloud providers and Fusion are opt-in.","Nothing is hidden. Inspect the prompt, replay trace drift, edit skills, and swap parts without waiting for a vendor. Plain local models, SQLite files, and NDJSON traces.","Runs on your hardware. Small quantized models run on everyday consumer GPUs and CPUs, no datacenter needed."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AtomicBot-ai/atomic-agent/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"7acc109bbdbf18793b50b3a428b57ed0b7e9f5e8ab8935ca0592a87b733cb52a","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:43.768Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:43.768Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A local-first AI agent that runs on your machine, with local or cloud models.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AtomicBot-ai/atomic-agent/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Prerequisite: the CLI installed and signed in: claude then /login, or npm i -g @openai/codex then codex login.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AtomicBot-ai/atomic-agent/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"For Claude that is sonnet, opus, haiku, fable, or a pinned id like claude-sonnet-5; for Codex leave it blank: under a ChatGPT login Codex rejects explicit model ids (not supported when using Codex with a ChatGPT account) and resolves one itself.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AtomicBot-ai/atomic-agent/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"7acc109bbdbf18793b50b3a428b57ed0b7e9f5e8ab8935ca0592a87b733cb52a","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AtomicBot-ai/atomic-agent/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:43.769Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T12:21:57Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AtomicBot-ai/atomic-agent/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T22:42:32.239Z","hash":"7acc109bbdbf18793b50b3a428b57ed0b7e9f5e8ab8935ca0592a87b733cb52a","originalBytes":64474,"storedBytes":64474,"truncated":false},"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:43.665Z","enrichmentAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T23:12:12.870Z","latestRelease":{"name":"v0.6.7","tag":"v0.6.7","publishedAt":"2026-10-07T14:46:28Z","url":"https://github.com/AtomicBot-ai/atomic-agent/releases/tag/v0.6.7"},"releas